## ================================
## .gitignore for ERP (ASP.NET Core)
## ================================
## This file tells Git which files/folders to IGNORE (not track).
## These are things that get auto-generated, are machine-specific,
## or contain sensitive/runtime data that shouldn't go into source control.


## ---- Build output ----
## Created every time you build the project. Not source code, so no need to track it.
bin/
obj/


## ---- Visual Studio files ----
## Editor/IDE settings specific to your machine, not the project itself.
.vs/
*.user
*.suo


## ---- Rider / VS Code (in case you or teammates use them) ----
.idea/
.vscode/


## ---- Uploaded files (resumes, documents, etc.) ----
## These are runtime data created by users of the app, not code.
## Keeping the folder structure but ignoring the actual files is common practice.
wwwroot/uploads/*
!wwwroot/uploads/.gitkeep


## ---- Logs ----
*.log
logs/


## ---- Sensitive / environment-specific settings ----
## appsettings.Development.json often has local DB connection strings, API keys, etc.
## Keep appsettings.json (with placeholder values) tracked, but ignore the local dev one.
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.local.json


## ---- Database files (if using local SQLite/LocalDB) ----
*.mdf
*.ldf
*.db


## ---- NuGet ----
*.nupkg
**/packages/*
!**/packages/build/

## ---- Node/npm (if you ever add front-end tooling) ----
node_modules/


## ---- OS-generated files ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
